═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════
ANIMATION SYSTEM (Apply across ALL components)
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════

In index.css define these custom CSS animations:
@keyframes float { 0%,100%{transform:translateY(0)} 50%{transform:translateY(-12px)} }
@keyframes pulse-glow { 0%,100%{box-shadow:0 0 20px var(--primary-color,#6366f1)} 
                         50%{box-shadow:0 0 40px var(--primary-color,#6366f1)} }
@keyframes gradient-shift { 0%{background-position:0% 50%} 
                             50%{background-position:100% 50%} 
                             100%{background-position:0% 50%} }

Framer Motion variants to use throughout (define in src/utils/variants.js):
export const fadeInUp = {
  hidden: { opacity: 0, y: 40 },
  visible: { opacity: 1, y: 0, transition: { duration: 0.6, ease: 'easeOut' } }
}
export const staggerContainer = {
  hidden: {},
  visible: { transition: { staggerChildren: 0.12 } }
}
export const slideFromLeft = {
  hidden: { opacity: 0, x: -60 },
  visible: { opacity: 1, x: 0, transition: { duration: 0.7, ease: 'easeOut' } }
}
export const slideFromRight = {
  hidden: { opacity: 0, x: 60 },
  visible: { opacity: 1, x: 0, transition: { duration: 0.7, ease: 'easeOut' } }
}
export const scaleIn = {
  hidden: { opacity: 0, scale: 0.85 },
  visible: { opacity: 1, scale: 1, transition: { duration: 0.5 } }
}

All sections: wrap with <motion.section variants={fadeInUp} initial="hidden" whileInView="visible" viewport={{ once: true, margin: '-100px' }}>

Page transitions: wrap routes in <AnimatePresence mode="wait"> with fade transition

Skeleton loaders: pulsing gray boxes matching the layout of actual content 
(use Tailwind animate-pulse with bg-white/10 rounded blocks)

═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════
RESPONSIVE DESIGN
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════

All sections fully responsive:
- Mobile (<768px): single column, hamburger nav, Three.js sections 
  show 2D fallback card grids (check window.innerWidth < 768, skip Three.js canvas)
- Tablet (768-1024px): two columns where applicable
- Desktop (>1024px): full multi-column layouts

Admin panel mobile: sidebar collapses to bottom drawer with hamburger toggle

═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════
FIRST-TIME SETUP FLOW
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════

1. User clones project, sets .env variables
2. Runs: cd server && npm install && npm start
         cd client && npm install && npm run dev
3. Visits /admin/login
4. First visit: shows "Setup Admin Account" form (email + password + ADMIN_SETUP_KEY)
   → POST /api/auth/setup → creates admin → redirects to /admin
5. From /admin: fills in all sections
6. Homepage at / shows live data immediately

Admin login page (/admin/login):
- If setup not done (no admin in DB), show setup form
- If setup done, show login form
- After login → redirect to /admin
- Forgot password: not needed (single user, they can reset via MongoDB directly — note in README)

═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════
MAINTENANCE MODE
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════

If SiteMeta.maintenanceMode = true:
- Homepage shows a full-screen "Coming Soon" page
  → Animated gradient background
  → Big text: "Something amazing is coming"
  → Small text: "Check back soon"
- Admin panel still accessible via /admin/login (not affected by maintenance mode)

